# Impeccable tooling output: review screenshots (scripts/shoot.mjs), critique
# snapshots, decision-page state and the detector hook cache. All generated,
# none of it source — durable design decisions live in packages/web-client-v3/DESIGN.md
# and docs/. Ignored as a whole directory rather than per-subdirectory, because
# review/ alone left critique/ and questions/ untracked-but-visible, which is a
# trap for a wide `git add -A`.
#
# ...EXCEPT config.json, which is not generated: it records reviewed decisions
# (which detector findings are false positives for this design system, and why).
# A blanket `.impeccable/` was right while everything inside was output; it now
# excludes the one file that IS source, so a "shared" suppression would be lost on
# a fresh clone and the hook would re-fire for the next reader.
# Note the pattern shape: `.impeccable/` excludes the directory itself, so git
# never descends and a negation inside it cannot match. `.impeccable/*` plus the
# negation is what actually works — verified with `git check-ignore -v`.
# `**/` is required: a bare `.impeccable/*` contains a slash and is therefore
# ANCHORED to the repo root, which silently un-ignored the second .impeccable
# directory under packages/web-client-v3/ (hook cache + review screenshots).
# Caught by reading `git status`, not by reasoning about the pattern.
**/.impeccable/*
!/.impeccable/config.json

# Playwright MCP output: screenshots, accessibility snapshots (.yml) and console
# logs, written to the repo root by the browser tools. Verified by observation
# rather than assumed — one navigate produced page-*.yml and console-*.log here.
# Ignored as a whole directory for the same reason as .impeccable/ above: a
# partially-ignored generated dir leaves the rest untracked-but-visible, which is
# a trap for a wide `git add -A`.
.playwright-mcp/

# Local dev env files (per-developer secrets)
**/.env.local
